  "method": "selected-public-voynich-msi-intake-v1",
  "observations": {
    "116v": "The processed view emphasizes dense faint reversed-looking writing across the otherwise pale body, in addition to the short upper writing and left-edge figures. The true-color views leave much of that body writing faint. The two PSC copies display oppositely when their EXIF orientations are honored. Upper writing contains a short separate upper row plus three longer rows in these views; no glyphs or words were newly transcribed.",
    "1r": "All three processed full frames show the same main writing blocks and mounting/chart/ruler context with different false-color palettes. Dark leaf-shaped forms overlap the writing area. Faint lower-margin writing and marks down the right margin are more conspicuous than in the separately framed Yale view, but individual readings and exact column alignment were not adjudicated at these reduced full-frame displays.",
    "disposition": "supplementary views; glyph readings and legacy alias unresolved"
  },
